== bridge: one schema per tenant ==

## 11. Bridge: one schema per tenant
   concept: same table names in every schema; per request the app sets search_path to the tenant's schema and the role to the tenant's role, both LOCAL
   hooli    runs as tenant_hooli, search_path t_hooli: invoices #1, #2
   initrode runs as tenant_initrode, search_path t_initrode: invoices #1, #1
   vandelay runs as tenant_vandelay, search_path t_vandelay: invoices #1
   check ok: each request runs as its tenant's role, in its tenant's schema

## 12. search_path is not a security boundary
   concept: schema-qualified names ignore search_path; only privileges stop them, so each tenant needs its own role and the app must switch to it
   one shared role, search_path t_hooli, SELECT FROM t_initrode.invoices: 2 rows of initrode's
   role tenant_hooli, same query: rejected: permission denied for schema t_initrode
   check ok: a schema-qualified name reaches another tenant under one shared role; the tenant's own role is denied

## 13. search_path and role leak on a pooled connection
   concept: pool of 1 connection: session-level settings stay on the connection, the next request inherits the previous tenant's schema and role
   request 1 (hooli): SET ROLE tenant_hooli; SET search_path = t_hooli (session level)
   request 2 (initrode, forgot the context): runs as tenant_hooli, sees 2 invoices (hooli's)
   check ok: session-level role and search_path leak hooli's context into the next request
   after DISCARD ALL (a pool reset query), request 1 (hooli): the same settings, LOCAL to its transaction
   request 2 (initrode, forgot the context): rejected: relation "invoices" does not exist (loud, where RLS returned zero rows)
   check ok: with LOCAL settings and DISCARD ALL, a request without context fails loudly

## 14. Every migration runs once per schema
   concept: migration 2 (add currency, UNIQUE (number)) loops over the schemas, one transaction each; tenant data differs, so one schema can fail and leave the fleet half migrated
     t_hooli: migrated to 2
     t_initrode: failed: could not create unique index "invoices_number_key" (Key (number)=(1) is duplicated.); loop stopped
   versions now: t_hooli 2, t_initrode 1, t_vandelay 1; the app must handle both shapes until every schema is done
   check ok: one schema's data stops the loop: the fleet is left half migrated
   fixed initrode's duplicate invoice number, re-ran the loop:
     t_hooli: already at 2, skipped
     t_initrode: migrated to 2
     t_vandelay: migrated to 2
   versions now: t_hooli 2, t_initrode 2, t_vandelay 2
   check ok: after the fix the re-run skips done schemas and migrates the rest

## 15. Catalog bloat at many tenants
   concept: every schema copies every table, index and sequence into the system catalogs; 1000 more tenants, then migration 2 across all of them
   3 tenants                        3 tenant schemas, pg_class 437 rows, pg_attribute 3228 rows, system catalogs 7776 kB
   1003 tenants                     1003 tenant schemas, pg_class 5437 rows, pg_attribute 30228 rows, system catalogs 20 MB
   migration 2 over 1000 more schemas: 6.7s, one transaction each (varies by machine)
   1003 tenants, after migration 2  1003 tenant schemas, pg_class 8437 rows, pg_attribute 43228 rows, system catalogs 25 MB
   check ok: every tenant schema adds relations to the catalog: pg_class grew by 8000 for 1000 tenants

