== silo: one database per tenant, and moving bigco out of the pool ==

## 16. Silo: one database per tenant
   concept: the directory maps each tenant to a database; the router opens a pool per database and the same code runs everywhere
   acme     -> pool: invoices 2, total 4600
   globex   -> pool: invoices 2, total 1490
   initech  -> silo_initech: invoices 2, total 6000
   umbrella -> silo_umbrella: invoices 1, total 9900
   check ok: the directory routes pooled tenants to pool and siloed ones to their own database

## 17. No path between databases
   concept: a connection is bound to one database; a bug in a query cannot reach another tenant's rows
   initech's connection reads silo_umbrella.public.invoices: rejected: cross-database references are not implemented: "silo_umbrella.public.invoices"
   check ok: a silo connection cannot read another tenant's database

## 18. What a silo costs
   concept: every database carries its own catalogs, and every database needs its own connections: connections are per database, a pool cannot share them
   on disk: pool 10 MB, silo_initech 7767 kB, silo_umbrella 7767 kB (pool holds 20000+ invoices, each silo 1 or 2)
   app connections with 5 busy requests per tenant: pool 5, silo_initech 5, silo_umbrella 5; max_connections 100
   every pooled tenant shares the pool database's connections; at 5 per silo, 20 silo tenants fill the server
   check ok: connections are per database: 5 busy requests per tenant hold 5 connections in each database

## 19. Deleting one tenant
   concept: umbrella leaves: in a silo that is one DROP DATABASE, not a DELETE ... WHERE tenant_id on every table followed by vacuum
   DROP DATABASE silo_umbrella; directory row removed
   umbrella request: rejected: unknown tenant umbrella
   check ok: deleting umbrella is one DROP DATABASE: the database and the directory row are gone

## 20. Moving a big tenant from the pool to a silo
   concept: pause bigco's writes, copy its rows by tenant_id into a new database, verify, flip the directory, delete it from the pool
   directory: bigco moving = true; bigco write: rejected: bigco is being moved: writes paused, reads still served by pool
   check ok: while bigco moves its writes are refused
   bigco read during the move: bigco    -> pool: invoices 20000, total 49990000
   copied into silo_bigco, ids kept: customers 1, invoices 20000
   verify: pool invoices 20000, total 49990000; silo_bigco invoices 20000, total 49990000
   check ok: the copy in silo_bigco has the same invoice count and total as the pool
   directory flipped: bigco -> silo_bigco, moving = false, statement_timeout 5000ms (no neighbors left to protect)
   bigco write, invoice 21001: ok, id 1
   bigco write, invoice 21002: ok, id 2
   bigco write, invoice 21003: ok, id 3
   bigco write, invoice 21004: rejected: duplicate key value violates unique constraint "invoices_pkey"
   check ok: the copied ids without their sequences collide on the 4th new invoice
   the copy kept the ids but not the sequences: they restarted at 1, ids 1-3 were free, 4 was taken. setval to max(id), with the tenant set (under forced RLS max(id) is NULL otherwise)
   bigco write: ok, invoice id 20004 in silo_bigco
   check ok: after setval, new invoices continue after the copied ids, in silo_bigco
   deleted from the pool: invoices 20000, customers 1
   acme     -> pool: invoices 2, total 4600
   bigco    -> silo_bigco: invoices 20004, total 49990400
   check ok: bigco now lives only in silo_bigco; acme still in the pool

